A||||7||Raydar||UPS (from Canada) question. Brokerage service charge?||||8||
Z||000000||Raydar||06-14-2001||09:50 AM||||Is anybody familiar with this? <BR>Bought a spoiler from Race Tech in Toronto. (Crappy quality, BTW), prepaid shipping. Several days after it arrived, I received a bill from UPS for a $19 "brokerage service charge".<BR>In another area of the form, they describe this as an "entry prep fee". <BR>Tariff Rate is free. Duty is $0.00. <BR>What did they do that I should pay them $19 for? I can't tell that they did a d@mn thing, other than deliver the box.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Is this reasonable? <BR>Shouldn't Race Tech at least tell me about this, since shipping was supposed to be "prepaid"? <P>[/rant]<P>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||billfredmike24||06-14-2001||12:26 PM||||It doesn't matter if you already paid shipping, I paid $110 "border fees" for a stereo i bought in the U.S.  It's UPS, never use them for cross border shipping, it's not Race-techs fault.  UPS checks the box for proper contents so it doesn't have to sit at the border and wait for customs to check it. It's bullshi$ as far as i'm concerned and am hesitant to buy things through the mail from the U.S.  Something can be double the price in Canada than the U.S, with the exchange rate it's still a lot cheaper, but once the custom fees are charged it ends up about the same price. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||beer_stud_21||06-14-2001||03:17 PM||||I send stuff to Canada fairly often via USPS for my dad's business.  To keep our customers from paying duty I under value the contents so that the customer only pays duty on the stated value, not what its really worth.  We run the risk of having the package getting lost in transit and not being able to get any money back but so far that hasn't happened.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||06-14-2001||03:49 PM||||What about listing something as a Birthday present?? what courrier service should be used???<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||06-14-2001||05:30 PM||||I use UPS for everything.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000005||kinboyatuwo||06-15-2001||01:19 AM||||You can avoid this but it takes some work.  First get the sender to write on the box, CUSTOMER WILL CLEAR CUSTOMS, then you refuse the package when it arrives and you will have to go to the ups depot (ask where) usually all big towns have one.  Then you get the import slip, bring it to customs and pay duty (usually really small) and taxes if applicable.  Then they stamp it and you bring it back to ups stamped and you can have your package.  Depending on where they are you decide.  They are close together here and it takes about 30 min to do it all and you save $$$$<P>email me if you have questions.  I am not familiar with some of the termonology but i can dig out papers if you need to know<P>kin<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/kinboyatuwo/kinboyatuwo.jpg">    <BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||4
Z||000006||Patrick's Dad||06-15-2001||07:43 PM||||I just got whacked with this, as well....<P>Bought a Preamp off eBay from a co. in Toronto. Got it two weeks ago, then got slapped with this bill.... Grrrr....||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||06-17-2001||01:35 AM||||Okay. <BR>Thanks to all that replied. I suppose that I'm not getting scammed, although it still <I>feels</I> like it. Guess I'll just go ahead and pay the damn thing, and not dispute it. <P>Jesse James used a gun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
